 excellence, the E-Class has secured a spot on the 2025 10Best and 2025 Editors Choice lists. For those seeking more power, the Mercedes-AMG E53 plug-in hybrid delivers an impressive 604 horsepower , catering to performance enthusiasts. New Features for 2025 The 2025 model introduces a new rear-wheel-drive E350 as the base variant, with 4Matic all-wheel drive available as an option and standard on the E450 . Safety enhancements include a center-mounted airbag , providing added protection for front-seat occupants in collisions. Additionally, a Patagonia Red exterior paint option and a faux-leather steering wheel have been introduced. 2025 Mercedes-Benz E-Class: Pricing and Best Trim to Choose The 2025 Mercedes-Benz E-Class starts at $63,500 and reaches $76,290 , depending on the trim and features: E350 $63,500 E350 Pinnacle (Recommended) $67,890 E450 $71,900 E450 Pinnacle $76,290 For a well-balanced combination of luxury and value, the E350 Pinnacle trim is recommended. It comes equipped with a 17-speaker Burmester audio system, head-up display, noise-insulating glass, illuminated grille, and ambient lighting . While the E350 lacks standard all-wheel drive , the 4Matic system can be added for $2,500 , improving traction and handling in various conditions. For those prioritizing power and refinement, the E450 with its smooth inline-six engine is a compelling choice. 2025 Mercedes-Benz E-Class: Engine, Transmission, and Performance The E350 features a turbocharged 2.0-liter four-cylinder engine with a 23-hp electric motor , generating 255 horsepower . The E450 , on the other hand, employs a turbocharged 3.0-liter inline-six engine with a hybrid system, producing 375 horsepower . These hybrid setups help reduce turbo lag and enhance fuel efficiency. Both engines provide a refined and quiet driving experience, with the E450 offering more power and a richer engine note. Related Articles 2025 Tesla Model S: Electric Super Sedan 3 weeks ago 2025 BMW 2-Series Gran Coupe Review May 12, 2025 2025 Cadillac CT4-V Blackwing: Pure Performance May 3, 2025 For superior ride quality, an adjustable air suspension is available as an upgrade over the standard steel-spring setup. Additionally, a rear-wheel steering system enhances maneuverability, particularly in tight spaces. Acceleration and Performance E350 4\', \'images\': [], \'rank\': 1}, {\'url\': \'https://carscounsel.com/mercedes-benz-e-class-best-worst/\', \'content\': \'Best and Worst Mercedes Benz E Class Years: What to Buy & Avoid CarsCounsel Skip to content Menu Home Glossary Calculators About Contact Menu Home Glossary Calculators About Contact Best and Worst Mercedes Benz E Class Years: What to Buy & Avoid David Lawrence April 4, 2025 As you delve into the Mercedes-Benz E-Class, youll find a mix of standout models and those that fell short . You might be drawn to the 2010 and 2014 models, which boasted impressive fuel efficiency and performance upgrades. But what about the models that didnt quite live up to expectations? The 2003 and 2007 models, for instance, lacked significant updates, making them less desirable. What sets the best E-Class models apart, and which are the years to avoid ? Quick Navigation Toggle Key Takeaways Exceptional Performance Years Interior Comfort and Technology Exterior Design Evolution Safety Ratings and Reliability Best Resale Value Years Top Resale Value Models Best Years to Buy Worst Reliability Issues Notable Engine Options Advanced Safety Features Interior Updates and Amenities COMAND Infotainment System Heated Seat Options Premium Sound Quality Aerodynamic Design Improvements Fuel Efficiency and Emissions Diesel Engine Option Low Emissions Performance Semi-Autonomous Driving Systems Model Years to Avoid Key Takeaways The 2010 model year is considered one of the best, with a facelift, improved fuel efficiency, and a perfect 5-star safety rating. The 2014 model year offers a range of engine options, excellent fuel economy, and low emissions, making it a popular choice. The 2015 model year is notable for its updated interior design, new dashboard , and support for Apple CarPlay and Android Auto. The 2003 model year is a good option for those prioritizing performance, with improved engine performance and handling for racing dynamics. The 2004-2007 model years may be considered the worst, with fewer advanced safety features and less impressive fuel efficiency compared to later models. Exceptional Performance Years In terms of exceptional performance , the Mercedes-Benz E-Class has had its fair share of standout years. If youre looking for racing dynamics , the 2003 E-Class is a great option, thanks to its improved engine performance and handling. For increased power outputs , the 2006 E-Class features a more powerful V6 engine, providing better acceleration and responsiveness. The 2010 E-Class received a facelift, resulting in improved fuel efficiency and performance. The 2014 E-Class offers a range of engine options, providing excellent fuel economy and low emissions. Each of these models offers a unique performance experience thats sure to thrill. Interior Comfort and Technology Step inside the Mercedes-Benz E-Class, and youll be enveloped in a world of comfort and technology. Youll be surrounded by luxury upholstery and ambient lighting, creating a serene atmosphere. Over the years, the E-Class has undergone significant updates to augment interior comfort and technology. Year Notable Interior Features 2005 Heated seats, premium sound system 2009 COMAND infotainment system 2012 Lane departure warning, blind-spot assist 2015 New dashboard design, updated materials 2018 Adaptive cruise control, active lane change assist These advancements have lifted the E-Class to a new level of sophistication, making it a haven of comfort and innovation. Exterior Design Evolution The Mercedes-Benz E-Class has undergone a significant transformation in its exterior design over the years, with each iteration building upon the previous one to create a more refined and aerodynamic silhouette . Youll notice angular lines and sleek profiles that give the E-Class a sporty yet sophisticated look. The 2002 model introduced a more aggressive front end, while the 2007 update brought a revised grille and bumper design. Later models, such as the 2011 and 2013, offered updated trim options and minor facelifts. The 2016 model took it to the next level with a drag coefficient of 0.23, maki\', \'images\': [], \'rank\': 2}, {\'url\': \'https://www.caranddriver.com/mercedes-benz/e-class\', \'content\': "Skip to Content Global Nav Search SUBSCRIBE SIGN IN RESEARCH CARS EXPERT REVIEWS SHOPPING TOOLS WHATS MY CAR WORTH? EXPERT-TESTED GEAR NEWS + STORIES MAINTENANCE HomeMercedes-BenzE-Class 2025 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 2019 2018 2017 2025 Mercedes-Benz E-Class 10 / 10 C/D RATING MARC URBANO|CAR AND DRIVER View Photos MSRP $63,600$76,290 Car and Driver Accolades What\'s this? Editors\' Choice 10Best AT A GLANCE OVERVIEW RANK WHAT\'S NEW PRICING ENGINE & PERFORMANCE 0-60 TIME FUEL ECONOMY INTERIOR INFOTAINMENT & TECH SAFETY WARRANTY & MAINTENANCE HIGHS Plush, deeply comfortable cabin, potent and smooth six-cylinder, sophisticated tech-forward interior. LOWS Limited cargo capacity, capacitive-touch controls can be frustrating, pricier than rivals. VERDICT The Mercedes-Benz E-class is anelegant and luxurious choice among midsize luxury sedana compelling high-end machine that rolls with a healthy dose of technology. Specs SEE ALL SPECS EPA MPG 2528 Combined Seating 5 Seats Cargo Capacity 13 Cubic Feet Powertrain Gas Drivetrain All-Wheel Drive, Rear-Wheel Drive Limited Warranty 4 Years/50,000 Miles By Mark Takahashi Overview The 2025 Mercedes-Benz E-class is a rich amalgam of refinement, comfort, and innovationone of the best examples of the luxury car breed. It\'s very much the midsize interpretation of the stately and posh S-Classwhich is saying a lotwith a corresponding increase in agility and maneuverability. Compared to the BMW 5 series and Audi A6, the E-Class is more luxurious and opulent inside, with a handsomely renderedif complicatedinfotainment system delivering all of the newest tech features. It\'s not as sporty or athletic as the BMW or Audi, but for most luxury clients, that\'s not a priority. Still, it displays enough finesse and style to win a spot on our 2025 10Best and 2025 Editors\' Choice lists. For the rare driver desiring more performance, the new Mercedes-AMG E53 plug-in hybrid model with 604 horsepower should easily satisfy. We review that model separately. Where This Vehicle Ranks #1 in Best Luxury Mid-Size Cars 1 Mercedes-Benz E-class STARTING AT: $63,600 2 Genesis G80 STARTING AT: $58,595 3 Audi A7 STARTING AT: $73,295 4 Audi A6 STARTING AT: $59,395 5 BMW 5-series STARTING AT: $59,875 6 Volvo S90 STARTING AT: $59,495 New! Compare the 2025 Mercedes-Benz E-class with the top vehicles in this segment with our new compare tool. COMPARE THE TOP CARS What\'s New for 2025? This year, the E-class gets a new base model in the form of a rear-wheel-drive E350 four-cylinder. Mercedes\' 4Matic all-wheel drive is available as an option and remains standard on the E450. A new center-mounted airbag is standard across the lineup and deploys between the two front-seat occupants in the event of an accident. Patagonia Red is a new exterior color option and a faux-leather steering wheel is also now available. Pricing and Which One to Buy The price of the 2025 Mercedes-Benz E-class starts at $63,600 and goes up to $76,290 depending on the trim and options. E350 $63,600 E350 Pinnacle $67,890 E450 $72,000 E450 Pinnacle $76,290 0 $25k $50k $75k $100k $125k In addition to the choice of four-cylinder E350 or six-cylinder E450 engine choices, the E-class also offers a few different trim levels with varying levels of equipment: Premium and Pinnacle. We\'d stick with the four-cylinder powertrain in the E350 and spend the savings on upgrading to the Pinnacle trim, as it adds a lot of luxuries. Pinnacle models come with a 17-speaker Burmester stereo system, a head-up display, noise-insulating window glass, an illuminated grille, and ambient interior lighting. The E350 is the only model that does not come with 4Matic all-wheel-drive as standard, so we recommend adding it for only $2,500, especially for those who desire more performance or traction in inclement weather. And well forgive you if you choose to shell out the extra coin for the E450 in order to get its silky inline-six-cylinder engine; its velvety smoothness enhance", \'images\': [], \'rank\': 3}, {\'url\': \'https://www.arrowheadmb.com/blog/what-is-the-agility-control-feature-in-the-new-mercedes-benz-e-class-sedans/\', \'content\': \'Understanding AGILITY CONTROL in the Latest Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedans New View all [528] AMG GT [2] from $116,905 AMG GT [9] from $117,190 C-Class [37] from $51,145 CLA [13] from $47,445 CLE [19] from $66,075 E-Class [32] from $67,845 EQB [6] from $57,275 EQE [4] from $84,125 EQS [2] from $113,845 eSprinter Cargo Van [1] from $63,983 G-Class [7] from $180,170 GLA [18] from $42,250 GLB [24] from $44,550 GLC [81] from $50,435 GLE [100] from $67,365 GLA [18] from $42,250 GLB [24] from $44,550 GLC [81] from $50,435 GLE [100] from $67,365 GLS [89] from $92,325 Metris Passenger Van [1] from $44,988 S-Class [16] from $127,585 SL-Class [7] from $113,950 Sprinter Cargo Van [57] from $54,945 Sprinter Passenger Van [1] from $83,773 Sprinter Upfitted Camper Van [2] from $139,980 Shopping Tools Mercedes-Benz Models Value Your Trade Get Approved Pre-Owned View all [108] Cars [34] Trucks [1] SUVs & Crossovers [72] Vans [1] Hybrid & Electric [62] Price Under $20,000 $20,000 - $25,000 Over $25,000 Features New Arrivals Nearly new Over 30 MPG Convertible All-wheel drive Moonroof Leather seats Heated seats Shopping Tools Certified Pre-Owned All Pre-Owned CPO Warranties and Benefits Pre-Owned SUVs Electrified Mercedes-Benz Electric Vehicles Specials Manager Specials Service Specials National Offers Finance Online Pre-Approval Finance Center Value Your Trade Schedule Test Drive Buy or Lease a Mercedes-Benz Service / Parts Our Services Schedule Appointment Parts The Mercedes-Benz App Tire Center Recall Information Why Mercedes-Benz Service Research Model Research Model Comparisons Showroom n+ Bikes Pre-Owned Vehicle Research Mercedes-Benz FAQs Mercedes-Benz FAQ Tariffs FAQ About Our Dealership Contact Us Our Team Testimonials Employment Areas We Serve Pre-Owned Car Dealer near Me Community Events at Mercedes-Benz of Arrowhead Our Blog Mercedes-Benz of Arrowhead Official Blog What is the AGILITY CONTROL Feature in the New Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedans? August 1, 2024 By Admin Posted in Mercedes-Benz E-Class Understanding AGILITY CONTROL in the Latest Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedans The new Mercedes-Benz E-Class sedans are equipped with the advanced AGILITY CONTROL feature, a sophisticated system designed to enhance comfort and performance. This technology adjusts the suspension in real-time based on driving conditions and the drivers style, providing a smoother, more stable ride. Whether navigating city streets or cruising on the highway, the E-Class sedans offer a superior driving experience. Visit Mercedes-Benz of Arrowhead in Peoria, AZ, to explore the latest E-Class models. View Our Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedan Inventory Contact Us AGILITY CONTROL: Comfort Meets Performance Mercedes-Benz has added the AGILITY CONTROL feature to the new E-Class sedans to deliver exceptional performance and comfort. It utilizes selective damping, automatically adjusting each shock absorber based on the road surface and the drivers actions. During stronger body motions, the system firms up the shock absorbers for sharper handling and stability. Conversely, it reduces damping rates during smoother driving for a more comfortable ride. This dynamic adjustment ensures that the E-Class offers both sporty agility and luxurious comfort, adapting to changing driving conditions. {Also Read: What Sound System Does the New Mercedes E-Class Use? } Key Performance Enhancements of Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedan In addition to the standard steel suspension, the new E-Class offers the AIRMATIC air suspension system as part of the Technology package. This advanced system includes ADS+ continuously adjustable damping and rear-axle steering. The AIRMATIC system uses air springs and adaptive dampers that adjust automatically for each wheel, responding to road quality to maintain ride comfort. It also features a level control function that adjusts ground clearance based on speed and load, reducing air resistance and improving fuel efficiency at higher speeds. This combination of technologie\', \'images\': [], \'rank\': 4}, {\'url\': \'https://www.mbusa.com/en/vehicles/class/e-class/sedan\', \'content\': "The Mid-Size E-Class Sedan | Mercedes-Benz USA Skip Navigation Back Search QUICK LINKS Mercedes Electric Build Your Own Special Offers New Inventory Mercedes Owners Certified Pre-Owned Vehicles Electric Shopping Owners My Account Find a Dealer Search Find a Dealer Back Vehicles All Vehicles Compare Vehicles Special Offers Certified Pre-Owned Program Future Vehicles Features & Education Plug-In Hybrid Vehicles (PHEV) AMG Electric Architecture (AMG.EA) Brands Mercedes-AMG Mercedes Electric Mercedes-Maybach Mercedes-Benz Vans Back Electric DISCOVER ELECTRIC Mercedes-Benz Electric Explore the Lineup Charging Your Vehicle Electric FAQs EV Charging Tools Shop Electric New Inventory Certified Pre-Owned All-Electric Special Offers Build Your Own Charge up in Luxury Mercedes-Benz High-Power Charging Network, a premium experience for effortless public charging and preferential access for Mercedes-Benz drivers across North America. Learn More About Charging Back Shopping INVENTORY New Vehicles Certified Pre-Owned Vehicles Pre-Owned Vehicles Special Offers Start Purchase Online TOOLS Build Your Own Shopping Assist Compare Vehicles Request a Quote Finance Financial Services Apply for Financing Trade-in Value Shopping Assist by Mercedes-Benz Answer a few quick questions and your selected dealer will find the perfect match for you. Find Your Dream Mercedes-Benz Back Owners Service & Manuals Owners Support Maintenance Support Owners Manuals Service & Warranty Manuals Schedule Service Updating your Vehicle Accessories Recall Information Vehicle Information Bluetec Update OWNERSHIP ON-THE-Go Mercedes-Benz App Mercedes-Benz Store Mercedes-Benz Finance App Back My Account Log In or Register Even if you dont own a Mercedes-Benz, you can register for an account to save builds, track inventory, set alerts and more. Login Register Explore Account Details View Account Saved Vehicles Deals In Progress Log Out Mercedes-Benz App The Mercedes-Benz app is the ultimate resource, putting control of your vehicle in the palm of your hand. Learn More Back Search QUICK LINKS Mercedes Electric Build Your Own Special Offers New Inventory Mercedes Owners Certified Pre-Owned Show Navigation E-Class Sedan The standard that never stands still View Inventory Gallery Models AMG E-Class Sedan Build E-Class Sedan AMG E-Class Sedan INNOVATION Few cars have as rich a sense of tradition as the E-Class. And foremost among its traditions is advancement, pioneering new ideas and redefining standards. With breakthroughs in connectivity, intelligence and user-friendly tech, it\'s an E-Class for your tomorrow. Starring role model The intuitive digital cockpit\'s two large screens include a 14.4-inch touchscreen. The Superscreen option adds a third display for the front passenger, plus a driver-facing camera usable for 3rd-party conferencing apps or even selfies. Disclaimer [5] Disclaimer [6] Virtual reality show The groundbreaking Mercedes-Benz User Experience (MBUX) marks its third generation with more advanced AI, for quicker response to your natural voice. The optional Head-Up Display helps keep key driving info closer to your natural line of sight. D