007 update brought a revised grille and bumper design. Later models, such as the 2011 and 2013, offered updated trim options and minor facelifts. The 2016 model took it to the next level with a drag coefficient of 0.23, maki', 'images': [], 'rank': 2}, {'url': 'https://www.caranddriver.com/mercedes-benz/e-class', 'content': \"Skip to Content Global Nav Search SUBSCRIBE SIGN IN RESEARCH CARS EXPERT REVIEWS SHOPPING TOOLS WHATS MY CAR WORTH? EXPERT-TESTED GEAR NEWS + STORIES MAINTENANCE HomeMercedes-BenzE-Class 2025 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 2019 2018 2017 2025 Mercedes-Benz E-Class 10 / 10 C/D RATING MARC URBANO|CAR AND DRIVER View Photos MSRP $63,600$76,290 Car and Driver Accolades What's this? Editors' Choice 10Best AT A GLANCE OVERVIEW RANK WHAT'S NEW PRICING ENGINE & PERFORMANCE 0-60 TIME FUEL ECONOMY INTERIOR INFOTAINMENT & TECH SAFETY WARRANTY & MAINTENANCE HIGHS Plush, deeply comfortable cabin, potent and smooth six-cylinder, sophisticated tech-forward interior. LOWS Limited cargo capacity, capacitive-touch controls can be frustrating, pricier than rivals. VERDICT The Mercedes-Benz E-class is anelegant and luxurious choice among midsize luxury sedana compelling high-end machine that rolls with a healthy dose of technology. Specs SEE ALL SPECS EPA MPG 2528 Combined Seating 5 Seats Cargo Capacity 13 Cubic Feet Powertrain Gas Drivetrain All-Wheel Drive, Rear-Wheel Drive Limited Warranty 4 Years/50,000 Miles By Mark Takahashi Overview The 2025 Mercedes-Benz E-class is a rich amalgam of refinement, comfort, and innovationone of the best examples of the luxury car breed. It's very much the midsize interpretation of the stately and posh S-Classwhich is saying a lotwith a corresponding increase in agility and maneuverability. Compared to the BMW 5 series and Audi A6, the E-Class is more luxurious and opulent inside, with a handsomely renderedif complicatedinfotainment system delivering all of the newest tech features. It's not as sporty or athletic as the BMW or Audi, but for most luxury clients, that's not a priority. Still, it displays enough finesse and style to win a spot on our 2025 10Best and 2025 Editors' Choice lists. For the rare driver desiring more performance, the new Mercedes-AMG E53 plug-in hybrid model with 604 horsepower should easily satisfy. We review that model separately. Where This Vehicle Ranks #1 in Best Luxury Mid-Size Cars 1 Mercedes-Benz E-class STARTING AT: $63,600 2 Genesis G80 STARTING AT: $58,595 3 Audi A7 STARTING AT: $73,295 4 Audi A6 STARTING AT: $59,395 5 BMW 5-series STARTING AT: $59,875 6 Volvo S90 STARTING AT: $59,495 New! Compare the 2025 Mercedes-Benz E-class with the top vehicles in this segment with our new compare tool. COMPARE THE TOP CARS What's New for 2025? This year, the E-class gets a new base model in the form of a rear-wheel-drive E350 four-cylinder. Mercedes' 4Matic all-wheel drive is available as an option and remains standard on the E450. A new center-mounted airbag is standard across the lineup and deploys between the two front-seat occupants in the event of an accident. Patagonia Red is a new exterior color option and a faux-leather steering wheel is also now available. Pricing and Which One to Buy The price of the 2025 Mercedes-Benz E-class starts at $63,600 and goes up to $76,290 depending on the trim and options. E350 $63,600 E350 Pinnacle $67,890 E450 $72,000 E450 Pinnacle $76,290 0 $25k $50k $75k $100k $125k In addition to the choice of four-cylinder E350 or six-cylinder E450 engine choices, the E-class also offers a few different trim levels with varying levels of equipment: Premium and Pinnacle. We'd stick with the four-cylinder powertrain in the E350 and spend the savings on upgrading to the Pinnacle trim, as it adds a lot of luxuries. Pinnacle models come with a 17-speaker Burmester stereo system, a head-up display, noise-insulating window glass, an illuminated grille, and ambient interior lighting. The E350 is the only model that does not come with 4Matic all-wheel-