s-Benz Service Research Model Research Model Comparisons Showroom n+ Bikes Pre-Owned Vehicle Research Mercedes-Benz FAQs Mercedes-Benz FAQ Tariffs FAQ About Our Dealership Contact Us Our Team Testimonials Employment Areas We Serve Pre-Owned Car Dealer near Me Community Events at Mercedes-Benz of Arrowhead Our Blog Mercedes-Benz of Arrowhead Official Blog What is the AGILITY CONTROL Feature in the New Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedans? August 1, 2024 By Admin Posted in Mercedes-Benz E-Class Understanding AGILITY CONTROL in the Latest Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedans The new Mercedes-Benz E-Class sedans are equipped with the advanced AGILITY CONTROL feature, a sophisticated system designed to enhance comfort and performance. This technology adjusts the suspension in real-time based on driving conditions and the drivers style, providing a smoother, more stable ride. Whether navigating city streets or cruising on the highway, the E-Class sedans offer a superior driving experience. Visit Mercedes-Benz of Arrowhead in Peoria, AZ, to explore the latest E-Class models. View Our Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedan Inventory Contact Us AGILITY CONTROL: Comfort Meets Performance Mercedes-Benz has added the AGILITY CONTROL feature to the new E-Class sedans to deliver exceptional performance and comfort. It utilizes selective damping, automatically adjusting each shock absorber based on the road surface and the drivers actions. During stronger body motions, the system firms up the shock absorbers for sharper handling and stability. Conversely, it reduces damping rates during smoother driving for a more comfortable ride. This dynamic adjustment ensures that the E-Class offers both sporty agility and luxurious comfort, adapting to changing driving conditions. {Also Read: What Sound System Does the New Mercedes E-Class Use? } Key Performance Enhancements of Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedan In addition to the standard steel suspension, the new E-Class offers the AIRMATIC air suspension system as part of 