n electric motor. The ride and handling benefit from a standard air-spring suspension, and heated and ventilated massaging front seats coddle the occupants. Well-equipped as standard, there's also a long list of optional hides, woods, and colors to personalize the S-class to your taste. If there is an area of contention, it's the sheer number of screens and their almost overwhelming amount of controls and features. Still, while many rivals including the Audi A8, BMW 7-series, and Genesis G90 have made inroads onto the big Benz's turf, for now at least, it remains the king of full-size luxury sedans. As one of our favorites in its segment, the Mercedes-Benz S-class has also earned a spot on our Editors Choice list for 2025. Where This Vehicle Ranks #1 in Best Full-Size Luxury Cars 1 Mercedes-Benz S-class STARTING AT: $118,900 2 Genesis G90 STARTING AT: $91,195 3 BMW 7-series STARTING AT: $98,475 4 Mercedes-AMG S-Class STARTING AT: $187,350 5 Audi A8 STARTING AT: $93,295 6 Audi S8 STARTING AT: $126,595 New! Compare the 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-class with the top vehicles in this segment with our new compare tool. COMPARE THE TOP CARS What's New for 2025? Mild updates arrive for 2025, including a center airbag and a standard digital key. New Verde Silver and Sonoran Brown exterior paint hues that fill in for the departing Mojave Silver and Onyx Black. The four-zone climate control, previously available only as part of a package, is now a standalone option; similarly, AMG Line trim is now a standalone package that can be added to the Luxury and Executive trims. Those looking for an even mightier, performance-focused model can check out the AMG S-class . And for those with money to burn, there's the Mercedes-Maybach S-class (both reviewed separately). Pricing and Which One to Buy The price of the 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-class starts at $118,900 and goes up to $129,750 depending on the trim and options. S500 $118,900 S580e $129,350 S580 $129,750 0 $50k $100k $150k $200k Once you pass the $100K point, economizing seems pointless. We suggest going for the S580 as it nets the big turbo V-8, not to mention Nappa leather upholsterysure the S500 has leather, but not Nappa leatherand a heated steering wheel as standard kit. Live a little. Want to compare the 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-class to other vehicles you're interest\", 'images': [], 'rank': 2}, {'url': 'https://www.mercedes-amg.com/en/s-class-sedan', 'content': '[error] Timeout while extracting content', 'rank': 3}, {'url': 'https://www.carsandhorsepower.com/reviews/exploring-the-features-of-the-2024-s-class', 'content': \"Exploring the Features of the 2024 S-Class Cars&Horsepower Home News Featured Reviews Buying Guides ABOUT Us Contact Us Privacy Policy / Terms of Use / Disclaimer Cars&Horsepower Home News Featured Reviews Buying Guides ABOUT Us Contact Us Privacy Policy / Terms of Use / Disclaimer Home Reviews Exploring the Features of the 2024 S-Class Exploring the Features of the 2024 S-Class 9 min read 30 Dec 30 Dec The 2024 S-Class is the latest flagship luxury sedan from Mercedes-Benz. It's a symbol of the brand's commitment to innovation, luxury, and performance. The S-Class has always been a benchmark in the automotive industry. The 2024 model continues this tradition, pushing boundaries in design, technology, and comfort. This article explores the features that make the 2024 S-Class stand out. We delve into its design evolution, technological advancements, and what sets it apart in the luxury car market. We'll look at the exterior and interior design, the cutting-edge infotainment system, and the advanced safety features. We'll also discuss the powertrain options and the role of electrification in the lineup. Whether you're a potential buyer, a car enthusiast, or just curious about the latest in high-end vehicle technology, this comprehensive overview is for you. See also: Mercedes-Benz Introduces The Definitive GLC 350e Plug-In Hybrid SUV For 2025 The Legacy of the S-Class Photo Cre