l-efficient Mercedes E-Class models: E-Class Fuel type Engine Claimed Fuel Efficiency Real-world Fuel Efficiency Power E200 Petrol 2.0T 7.2 L/100 Km 39 MPG UK 33 MPG US 7.80 L/100 Km 36.2 MPG UK 30.2 MPG US 197 hp E200d Diesel 1.6T 4.9 L/100 Km 58 MPG UK 48 MPG US 6.0 L/100 Km 47.1 MPG UK 39.2 MPG US 160 hp E300e Plug-in hybrid petrol 2.0T 1.6 L/100 Km 177 MPG UK 147 MPG US 5.66 L/100 Km 49.9 MPG UK 41.6 MPG US 320 hp E300de Plug-in hybrid diesel 2.0T 1.2 L/100 Km 235 MPG UK 196 MPG US 4.67 L/100 Km 60.5 MPG UK 50.4 MPG US 306 hp 1. The most fuel-efficient petrol: W213 E200 Lets start with the most efficient Mercedes E-Class with a petrol engine, the W213 E200! The W213 generation of the Mercedes E-Class has been in production since 2016, but it received a facelift in 2021. The E200 is equipped with a turbocharged four-cylinder petrol engine, capable of returning an official combined fuel economy of 7.2 L/100 Km / 39 MPG UK / 33 MPG US, despite having a power output of 197 horsepower. However, as we all know, the claimed fuel economy of a car can be a whole lot different compared to what you can actually achieve in practice. So, how good is the Mercedes E200s fuel efficiency in the real world? To check this, we will use Spritmonitor.de , where car owners monitor their fuel consumption and add them to the database. When filtering on the W213 Mercedes E200, we see an average fuel consumption of 7.80 L/100 Km / 36.2 MPG UK / 30.2 MPG US, which is quite close to the claimed fuel economy! Reported real-world fuel economy of the W213 E200 from 12 different owners Here is an example of the fuel consumption experienced by a single owner over a distance of 17,002 kilometers: Source 2. The most fuel-efficient diesel: W213 E200d The W213 E200d is a marvel of efficiency. Using a turbocharged four-inline diesel engine, the E200ds claimed combined fuel economy is 4.9 L/100 Km / 58 MPG UK / 48 MPG US. Because of this great fuel economy and a 66-liter fuel tank, the E200d can get over 1,300 kilometers / 800 miles on a single tank, making it one of the most fuel-efficient cars on the road. But do these claimed figures represent the real world? Lets take a look! Reported real-world fuel economy of the W213 E200d from 20 different owners Spritmonitor shows that E200\', \'images\': [], \'rank\': 2}, {\'url\': \'https://www.fueleconomy.gov/feg/bymodel/2021_Mercedes-Benz_E-Class.shtml\', \'content\': "Gas Mileage of 2021 Mercedes-Benz E-Class Skip to main content Mobile Espaol Site Map General Links FAQ Videos Toggle navigation Find a Car Searches Find a Car Home Compare Side by Side Power Search Search by Make Hybrids, Diesels, and Alternative Fuel Cars Find a SmartWay Vehicle Best and Worst Vehicles Fueleconomy.gov Top Ten Today\'s Most Viewed Vehicles Used Car Label Fuel Economy Guides Print the Guide Help Promote Fuel Economy Find a Car Home Find a fuel efficient vehicle that meets your needs Used Car Label Selling your car? We can help you advertise its mpg. Save Money & Fuel Gas Mileage Tips Driving More Efficiently Keeping Your Car in Shape Planning and Combining Trips Choosing a More Efficient Vehicle Tips for Hybrids, Plug-in Hybrids, and Electric Vehicles Fuel Economy in Cold Weather Fuel Economy in Hot Weather More Information Tax Incentives Credits for New Vehicles Purchased in 2023 or After Credits for Pre-Owned Vehicles Purchased in 2023 or After Credits for New Vehicles Purchased Before 2023 Frequently Asked Questions Gasoline Prices Local Prices Questions About Gas Prices Cost Calculators Fuel Savings Calculator Trip Calculator Can a Hybrid Save Me Money? My Plug-in Hybrid Calculator Benefits Why is fuel economy important? Save Money Climate Change Oil Dependence Costs Sustainability Vehicles produce about half of the greenhouse gases from a typical U.S. household. My MPG My MPG - Home We can help you calculate and track your fuel economy. MPG Estimates from Others MPG estimates from drivers like you! Advanced Cars & Fuels About Hyb