            "text": "[{'url': 'https://www.arrowheadmb.com/blog/safety-features-of-the-2024-mercedes-benz-e-class/', 'content': 'Your Guide to the Safety Features of the 2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedan New View all [528] AMG GT [2] from $116,905 AMG GT [9] from $117,190 C-Class [37] from $51,145 CLA [13] from $47,445 CLE [19] from $66,075 E-Class [32] from $67,845 EQB [6] from $57,275 EQE [4] from $84,125 EQS [2] from $113,845 eSprinter Cargo Van [1] from $63,983 G-Class [7] from $180,170 GLA [18] from $42,250 GLB [24] from $44,550 GLC [81] from $50,435 GLE [100] from $67,365 GLA [18] from $42,250 GLB [24] from $44,550 GLC [81] from $50,435 GLE [100] from $67,365 GLS [89] from $92,325 Metris Passenger Van [1] from $44,988 S-Class [16] from $127,585 SL-Class [7] from $113,950 Sprinter Cargo Van [57] from $54,945 Sprinter Passenger Van [1] from $83,773 Sprinter Upfitted Camper Van [2] from $139,980 Shopping Tools Mercedes-Benz Models Value Your Trade Get Approved Pre-Owned View all [108] Cars [34] Trucks [1] SUVs & Crossovers [72] Vans [1] Hybrid & Electric [62] Price Under $20,000 $20,000 - $25,000 Over $25,000 Features New Arrivals Nearly new Over 30 MPG Convertible All-wheel drive Moonroof Leather seats Heated seats Shopping Tools Certified Pre-Owned All Pre-Owned CPO Warranties and Benefits Pre-Owned SUVs Electrified Mercedes-Benz Electric Vehicles Specials Manager Specials Service Specials National Offers Finance Online Pre-Approval Finance Center Value Your Trade Schedule Test Drive Buy or Lease a Mercedes-Benz Service / Parts Our Services Schedule Appointment Parts The Mercedes-Benz App Tire Center Recall Information Why Mercedes-Benz Service Research Model Research Model Comparisons Showroom n+ Bikes Pre-Owned Vehicle Research Mercedes-Benz FAQs Mercedes-Benz FAQ Tariffs FAQ About Our Dealership Contact Us Our Team Testimonials Employment Areas We Serve Pre-Owned Car Dealer near Me Community Events at Mercedes-Benz of Arrowhead Our Blog Mercedes-Benz of Arrowhead Official Blog Your Guide to the Safety Features of the 2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedan December 14, 2023 By Admin Posted in Mercedes-Benz E-Class Safety Features of the 2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedan Hey there, fellow road enthusiasts! Have you ever wondered how safe youd feel behind the 2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedan? Well, buckle up because were about to take a ride through its top-notch safety features that make driving not just a journey but a worry-free experience.Join us in this blog by Mercedes Benz Arrowhead as we take a deeper dive. Check Our Pre-owned Inventory Contact Mercedes-Benz of Arrowhead Sales Team [Read: Does the 2023 Mercedes-Benz E-Class have the MBUX feature? ] Avoiding Bumps with Smart Collision Prevention Imagine youre on the freeway, and traffic suddenly hits the brakes. No worriesthe E-Class Sedan has got your back. Its excellent collision prevention system taps into futuristic tech, gently slowing you down to dodge potential fender-benders. Its like having a co-pilot thats all about safety. 360-Degree Safety Hug Safety isnt just about whats in front of you, right? The 2024 E-Class Sedan agrees. This ride wraps you in a 360-degree safety hug thanks to its super-smart cameras and sensors. It keeps you in the loop about possible hazards from every angle, making you feel like youve got eyes in the back of your head (well, almost). Smart Buddy for the Road Meet your new road buddythe E-Class Sedan. Its not just a car; its also a brain! Smart driver assistance systems use fancy AI to study your driving habits and the world around you. From keeping you in your lane to cruising quickly, its like having a tech-savvy co-pilot who has your back, front, and sides. [Read: Driver Assistance Package in the 2023 Mercedes-Benz E-Class: Whats Included? ] Sidekick for Side Collisions Now, lets talk about sideswipes. The E-Class Sedan has this cool trick called the Mercedes-Benz PRE-SAFE Impulse Side. In case of a side collision, it inflates the front seats bolster lightning-fast, nudging you away from the hit. Its like having a superhero sidekick for your car. Miles of Zen A', 'images': [], 'rank': 1}, {'url': 'https://www.drivedata.org/car-safety-ratings/l/1239/mercedes-benz-e-class-2024', 'content': \"2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class Safety Ratings and Crash Test Results Vehicle Overview The 2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class blends advanced technology with refined comfort, continuing its tradition as a benchmark in the midsize luxury sedan segment. The latest model features updated exterior styling, a sophisticated interior with a large digital display, and an array of driver assistance systems. Turbocharged engines deliver a balance of power and efficiency, while available all-wheel drive enhances handling and traction. With spacious seating, premium materials, and the latest infotainment options, the E-Class offers a well-rounded experience for both drivers and passengers. Make: Mercedes-Benz Model: E-Class Year: 2024 Body Style: Sedan - 4 Door Vehicle Type: Passenger Car Drive Train: RWD Production Release: Early Release Vehicle Class: Body Frame: Number of Seats: 5 Seat Locations: 1,3,4,5,6 Seat Comments: Curb Weight: lbs Gross Weight Range: 5400.00 5700.00 lbs . . Overall Safety Ratings The 2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class is equipped with a comprehensive suite of safety features designed to enhance driver confidence and passenger protection. It includes multiple airbags strategically placed around the cabin, including front, side, and curtain airbags to provide extensive protection in the event of a collision. The vehicle comes standard with advanced driver assistance systems, such as collision prevention assist, which uses sensors to alert the driver of potential forward collisions and can autonomously apply brakes if necessary. Lane Keeping Assist helps prevent unintentional lane departures by gently steering the car back into its lane when it detects drifting. The E-Class is also outfitted with a cutting-edge Pre-Safe System, which anticipates certain collisions and prepares the cabin by tightening seatbelts and adjusting headrests for optimal safety. A crash data recorder is incorporated to log crucial information in the event of an accident. Additionally, seatbelt pretensioners automatically tighten belts to reduce slack during a frontal impact, offering enhanced protective measures to occupants. Advanced safety technology further includes blind-spot monitoring and a 360-degree camera system, which provide greater awareness of the vehicle's surroundings, making the 2024 E-Class a solid choice for those prioritizing safety. Overall Rating: Front Crash Rating (Overall): Side Crash Rating (Overall): Rollover Rating: Rollover Possibility: 0.00 Static Stability Factor: 0.00 Dynamic Tip Result: Other Years for the Mercedes-Benz E-Class | Vehicle | Body Style | Drive Train | Overall Stars Rating (1-5) | Frontal Impact Driver Stars Rating | Side Impact Driver Stars Rating | Rollover Impact Star Rating | |---|---|---|---|---|---|---| | 2018 Mercedes-Benz E-Class | Sedan - 4 Door | RWD | 5.00 | 5.00 | 5.00 | 5.00 | | 2022 Mercedes-Benz E-Class | Sedan - 4 Door | RWD | 5.00 | 4.00 | 5.00 | 5.00 | | 2014 Mercedes-Benz E-Class | Wagon | RWD | 4.00 | 4.00 | 5.00 | 5.00 | | 2018 Mercedes-Benz E-Class | Sedan - 4 Door | 4WD | 5.00 | 5.00 | 5.00 | 5.00 | | 2017 Mercedes-Benz E-Class | Sedan - 4 Door | RWD | 5.00 | 5.00 | 5.00 | 5.00 | Mercedes-Benz E-Class safety ratings. Frontal Crash Test Results Test Number: Test VIN: Driver Rating: Passenger Rating: Airbags Used: Safety Concerns (Driver): Safety Concerns (Passenger): Footnotes (Driver): Footnotes (Passenger): Injury Measures (Driver): HIC15: Chest Deflection: mm Left Femur Load: Right Femur Load: NIJ: Neck Tension: Neck Compression: Injury Measures (Passenger): HIC15: Chest Deflection: mm Left Femur Load: Right Femur Load: NIJ: Neck Tension: Neck Compression: Side Impact Test Results Test Number: Test VIN: Driver Rating: Passenger Rating: Barrier Star Rating: Combined Front Rating: Combined Rear Rating: Side Crash Airbags: Safety Concern (Driver): Safety Concern (Passenger): Footnotes (Driver): Footnotes (Passenger): Injury Measures (Driver): HIC36: Rib Deflection: Abdomen Force: Symphysis For\", 'images': [], 'rank': 2}, {'url': 'https://www.caranddriver.com/mercedes-benz/e-class-2024', 'content': \"2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class Review, Pricing, and Specs Search Cars By Category Expert Reviews Car Buying Guide Shopping Tools and Advice Car Buying Service Stories and Features News Expert-Tested Gear New Cars Follow Podcast Videos Subscribe to the Magazine About Us Newsletter Privacy Notice Terms Of Use Skip to Content Research Cars Expert Reviews Shopping Tools WHATS MY CAR WORTH? Expert-Tested Gear News + Stories Maintenance Follow Car and Driver Subscribe to the magazine About Us Contact Us Global Nav Search Subscribe sign in Research Cars Expert Reviews Shopping Tools WHATS MY CAR WORTH? Expert-Tested Gear News + Stories Maintenance Home Mercedes-Benz E-class 2024 2025 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 2019 2018 2017 2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class 9.5 / 10 C/D RATING Marc Urbano | Car and Driver Marc Urbano | Car and Driver Marc Urbano | Car and Driver Marc Urbano | Car and Driver View Photos Marc Urbano | Car and Driver MSRP $63,450$73,540 HIGHS Sweetly smooth ride, richly refined inline-six, a cocoon of luxury inside. LOWS Tech features more gimmicky than useful, finicky touch-sensitive controls, more expensive than the old model. VERDICT The new E-class blurs the line between mid-size and S-class-size, and carries into this new generation with grace and abundant luxury. Specs See all specs EPA MPG 2527 Combined Seating 5 Seats Cargo Capacity 19 Cubic Feet Powertrain Gas Drivetrain All-Wheel Drive Limited Warranty 4 Years/50,000 Miles By Drew Dorian Overview The E-class sedan is executive transport with a distinctly Mercedes-Benz attitude, offering nearly as much class and substance as the S-class flagship with a slightly less imposing profile. Entry-level E350 models are powered by a turbocharged 2.0-liter four-cylinder powertrain with 255 horsepower while E450s turn up the heat to 375 horsepower courtesy of a turbocharged 3.0-liter inline-six. Both powertrains deliver good punch and surprisingly good fuel economy. All-wheel drive is standard, and all models come luxuriously equipped and include a generous list of driver-assistance and infotainment featuressome of which are more gimmicky than useful. Other European rivals like the Audi A6 and the BMW 5-series offer similar space and equipment but neither brand has quite the prestige that comes with a Mercedes-Benz badge. What's New for 2024? This year marks the start of an all-new generation of the E-class sedan, which has been redesigned from the ground up with more technology and luxury than the outgoing model. The four- and six-cylinder powertrains have received hybrid assistance this year resulting in power boosts, and the exterior styling wears a handsome new look. Inside, a host of new technology features pepper the cabin. Pricing and Which One to Buy The price of the 2024 Mercedes-Benz E-class starts at $63,450 and goes up to $73,540 depending on the trim and options. E 350 $63,450 E350 Pinnacle $67,740 E 450 $69,250 E450 Pinnacle $73,540 In addition to the choice of four-cylinder E350 or six-cylinder E450 engine choices, the E-class also offers a few different trim levels with varying levels of equipment: Premium and Pinnacle. We'd stick with the four-cylinder powertrain in the E350 and spend the savings on upgrading to the Pinnacle trim, as it adds a lot of luxuries. Pinnacle models come with a 17-speaker Burmester stereo system, a head-up display, noise-insulating window glass, an illuminated grille, and ambient interior lighting. Want to compare the 2024 Mercedes-Benz E-class to other vehicles you're interested in? Our new compare tool provides a comprehensive, side-by-side look at up to five cars of your choice. Compare Cars Engine, Transmission, and Performance Under the E350's hood is a turbocharged 2.0-liter four-cylinder engine that pairs with a 23-hp electric motor for a combined 255 horsepower. The E450 model gets a similar hybrid setup for its turbocharged 3.0-liter inline-six, which brings the total to 375 horsepower. The hybrid systems are said to reduce turbo l\", 'images': [], 'rank': 3}, {'url': 'https://www.kbb.com/mercedes-benz/e-class/2024/specs/', 'content': \"2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class Specs & Feature Comparisons | Kelley Blue Book Car Values Price New/Used My Car's Value Instant Cash Offer Cars for Sale Cars for Sale Free Dealer Price Quote Vehicle History Report Find Local Dealers Private Seller Exchange Private Seller Cars Sell Your Car Shop & Buy Best Cars Dealer Reviews KBB Expert Reviews Electric Vehicle Guide KBB Awards Latest Car News Shopping & Buying Research Tools Car Research Browse Incentives Car Loan Calculator Car Finder Compare Cars Car Loans Insurance Check My Credit Extended Warranty Vehicle History Report Car Repair Auto Repair Prices Car Recalls Maintenance Pricing Find an Auto Shop Service Advisor OBD-II Codes Home Mercedes-Benz Mercedes-Benz E-Class 2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class Specs and Features 2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class Specs, Features & Options Here's everything you need to know about each trim in the 2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class lineup. Compare pricing, specs, key features and more. More About the 2024 Mercedes-Benz E-class Sedan Wagon Save 1 of 2 E-Class E 350 4MATIC Save 2 of 2 E-Class E 450 4MATIC See Pricing See Cars in Stock See Pricing See Cars in Stock MSRP $63,450 $69,250 Fuel Economy City 24/Hwy 33/Comb 27 MPG City 22/Hwy 31/Comb 25 MPG Fuel Type Gas Gas 5 Year Cost to Own 5-Year Cost to Own includes out of pocket expenses like fuel and insurance, plus the cars loss in value over time (depreciation). $82,624 $104,519 Horsepower 255 @ 5800 RPM 375 @ 5800 RPM Engine 4-Cyl, MHEV, Turbo, 2.0 Liter 6-Cyl, MHEV, Turbo, 3.0 Liter Cargo Volume 19.10 cu ft 19.10 cu ft Cylinders 4 6 Torque 295 lb-ft 369 lb-ft Turning Circle 36.5 feet 36.5 feet 5 Year Cost to Own Out of Pocket Expenses Fuel $10,135 $10,956 Maintenance $7,355 $9,387 Insurance $8,100 $21,060 Repairs $1,754 $1,754 Financing $9,210 $10,194 State Fees $8,267 $9,010 Total Out of Pocket Expenses $44,821 $62,361 Depreciation (Loss in Value) $37,803 $42,158 5 Year Cost to Own $82,624 $104,519 Safety Features Blind-Spot Alert Standard Standard Collision Warning System Standard Standard Driver Attention Assist Monitor Standard Standard Child Seat Anchors Standard Standard Child Door Locks Standard Standard Traction Control Standard Standard Surround View Camera Standard Standard Technology Bluetooth Wireless Technology Standard Standard Cruise Control Standard Standard Remote Keyless Entry Standard Standard Remote Engine Start Standard Standard Smartphone Interface Standard Standard Navigation System Standard Standard Voice Recognition System Standard Standard Touch Screen Monitor Standard Standard Hands Free Phone Standard Standard Entertainment Premium Radio Optional Optional Bluetooth Streaming Audio Standard Standard Bluetooth Wireless Technology Standard Standard Satellite Radio Standard Standard Comfort & Convenience Remote Control Liftgate/Trunk Release Standard Standard Remote Keyless Entry Standard Standard Cruise Control Standard Standard Bluetooth Streaming Audio Standard Standard Heated Mirrors Standard Standard Heated Steering Wheel Optional Optional Integrated Garage Door Opener Standard Standard Performance Torque 295 @ 5800 RPM 369 @ 5800 RPM 0 to 60 6.1 seconds 4.4 seconds Top Speed 130 mph 130 mph Seating Leather Seats Optional Optional Folding Rear Seat Standard Standard Dual Power Front Seats Standard Standard Power Driver's Seat Standard Standard Interior Leather-Wrapped Steering Wheel Standard Standard Power Outlet Optional Optional Power Windows Standard Standard Rear Window Defroster Standard Standard Steering Wheel Controls Standard Standard Tilt Steering Wheel Standard Standard Tilt/Telescoping Steering Wheel Standard Standard Cup Holder Count Standard Standard Exterior Adaptive Headlights Standard Standard Alloy Wheels Standard Standard Panorama Moon Roof Standard Standard Power Folding Exterior Mirrors Standard Standard Privacy Glass Standard Standard Rear Spoiler Optional Optional Rain Sensing Windshield Wipers Standard Standard Security Alarm System Standard Standard Mechanic\", 'images': [], 'rank': 4}, {'url': 'https://www.businessinsider.com/mercedes-benz-e-class-review-cool-tech-luxury-safety-features-2024-9?op=1', 'content': \"21 Features That Make the Mercedes E450 a High-Tech Luxury Beast - Business Insider Business Insider Subscribe Newsletters Search Business Strategy Economy Finance Retail Advertising Careers Media Real Estate Small Business The Better Work Project Personal Finance Tech Science AI Enterprise Transportation Startups Innovation Markets Stocks Indices Commodities Crypto Currencies ETFs Lifestyle Entertainment Culture Travel Food Health Parenting Politics Military & Defense Law Education Reviews Tech Streaming Tickets Home Kitchen Style Beauty Gifts Deals Video Big Business Food Wars So Expensive Still Standing Boot Camp Subscribe My account Log in Newsletters US edition Deutschland & sterreich Espaa Japan Netherlands Polska Get the app Transportation I drove an $88,000 Mercedes-Benz sedan. These 21 features make it one of the most high-tech luxury cars money can buy By Benjamin Zhang The 2024 Mercedes-Benz E450 sedan at Mercedes-Benz USA headquarters in Atlanta. Benjamin Zhang/Business Insider 2024-09-20T09:03:02Z Share Facebook Email X LinkedIn Copy link lighning bolt icon An icon in the shape of a lightning bolt. Impact Link Save Saved Read in app This story is available exclusively to Business Insider         subscribers. Become an Insider and start reading now. Have an account? Log in . The Mercedes-Benz E-Class is among the most iconic names in midsize luxury sedans. I recently reviewed a 2024 Mercedes-Benz E450 mild-hybrid luxury sedan. I was impressed by the E450's mild-hybrid engine, refined cabin, and immersive tech experience. The Mercedes-Benz E-Class is a stalwart in the midsize luxury sedan segment. This year, Mercedes launched the sixth-generation E-Class sedan, known internally as the W214. The new E-Class comes with fresh styling, new tech, and updated engine options. I recently reviewed a 2024 Mercedes-Benz E450 4Matic sedan with an as-tested price of $87,920. I was impressed by my Verde Silver Metallic test car's smooth, mild-hybrid powertrain, refined cabin, and immersive tech experience. Overall, the new E-Class artfully blends elements of traditional luxury with the latest in advanced safety and infotainment technology. The base E-350 starts at $62,300, while my six-cylinder 4Matic starts at $68,100. Here's a closer look at some of the E450's coolest features that make it a luxury automotive icon: 1. Fresh looks The new 2024 E450's revised looks. Benjamin Zhang/Business Insider The 2024 E-Class features updated front and rear fascias. The new front grille features a large Mercedes-Benz three-pointed star logo surrounded by a constellation of smaller three-pointed stars set against a black background. The design evokes the look of the brand's EQ-line of EVs. The redesigned rear end features stylized three-pointed stars embedded into the LED taillights. The rear bumper features a chrome-accented lower diffuser and a pair of exhaust outlets. Overall, the E-Class is a solid blend of modern looks and features while maintaining the stately elegance that has defined the brand for over a century. 2. Mild-hybrid engine The E450's 3.0 liter, turbocharged inline six-cylinder engine. Benjamin Zhang/Business Insider The Mercedes-Benz E-Class is available with two engine options. The base E350 sedan is powered by a 255-horsepower, 2.0-liter turbocharged inline-four-cylinder engine. My pricier E450 gets a 3.0-liter turbocharged inline-six-cylinder engine that produces 375 horsepower and 369 lb-ft of torque. Both engines are supplemented by Mercedes' 48-volt mild-hybrid system, which can contribute an additional 23 horsepower and 151 lb-ft of torque. The system is designed to mitigate the effects of turbo lag and quicken the response of its auto start/stop system. With 375 Teutonic ponies under the hood, the E450 is capable of sprinting from 0-60mph in a sports-car-shaming 4.4 seconds, according to Mercedes. My six-cylinder E450 test car boasts EPA fuel economy figures of 22 mpg city, 31 mpg highway, and 25 mpg combin\", 'images': [], 'rank': 5}, {'url': 'https://www.iihs.org/ratings/vehicle/mercedes-benz/e-class-4-door-sedan/2024', 'content': '[not extracted] Content limit reached', 'rank': 6}]",
